{"id": "lm-04", "kind": "limit_abuse", "tool": "run_sql", "args": {"sql": "SELECT 1", "limit": "5"}, "expect": "reject", "stricter_by_design": "the declared type is integer, so a string is rejected; the bare service calls int() on it", "note": "limit as a numeric string"}
{"id": "lm-05", "kind": "limit_abuse", "tool": "run_sql", "args": {"sql": "SELECT 1", "limit": true}, "expect": "reject", "stricter_by_design": "bool is an int in Python, so the bare service reads True as 1; the tool rejects it", "note": "boolean limit would mean one row"}
{"id": "lm-06", "kind": "limit_abuse", "tool": "run_sql", "args": {"sql": "SELECT 1", "limit": 2.5}, "expect": "reject", "stricter_by_design": "the declared type is integer; the bare service truncates 2.5 to 2 with int()", "note": "fractional limit"}
